  "articleBody": "It’s super common to wonder when the right time is to get a lawyer involved after an accident. Many folks think they can handle the initial steps themselves, but honestly, waiting too long can really hurt your case. The other party's insurance company often moves fast to minimize what they owe, so you want someone on your side just as quickly.\n\nFirst, if you've been injured at all, even if it seems minor, it’s a good idea to chat with an attorney. What feels minor now can develop into something much more serious later. Second, if the insurance company starts calling you within days, that's a huge red flag to get legal advice before saying anything. They're usually trying to get a recorded statement or push a quick, low settlement. Third, if you're unsure about your rights or what your claim is really worth, a lawyer can provide clarity. Finally, if you're facing any complex issues like multiple vehicles, serious injuries, or disputes about who was at fault, definitely don't go it alone.\n\nDon’t hesitate to reach out for a free consultation to understand your options. It costs nothing to get some expert advice and can make a world of difference for your recovery.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-26"
